2a:["$","$L42",null,{"children":[["$","$L43",null,{"title":"Timeouts under load, fine when idle","id":"timeouts-under-load-fine-when-idle","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Too much in flight. Lower ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_client_permits"}]," so work queues in Forge\ninstead of piling onto a single-threaded Redis. Only after that, consider\nraising ",["$","code",null,{"children":"command_timeout_ms"}],"."]}]}],["$","$L43",null,{"title":"Large blobs time out, small ones don't","id":"large-blobs-time-out-small-ones-dont","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"read_chunk_size"}]," is too large for the round-trip time to this Redis: one\ncommand is moving more data than fits in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"command_timeout_ms"}],". Lower the chunk\nsize."]}]}],["$","$L43",null,{"title":"Redis runs out of memory","id":"redis-runs-out-of-memory","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Forge does not evict from Redis; that's the instance's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"maxmemory"}]," and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"maxmemory-policy"}],". The one knob on this side is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"key_ttl_s"}],", which puts an\nexpiry on every key the store writes (meant for stores whose consumer can\nstop, not for scheduler state). Set the Redis-side limits, and reconsider\nwhether the bulk CAS should live here at all. For large blobs, a filesystem or object store tier is both\ncheaper and better suited."]}]}],["$","$L43",null,{"title":"Connection failures against a sentinel or cluster setup","id":"connection-failures-against-a-sentinel-or-cluster-setup","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Check ",["$","code",null,{"children":"mode"}],". For ",["$","code",null,{"children":"sentinel"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"addresses"}]," must hold exactly one sentinel URL,\nnot a data node, and the master name must match your sentinel configuration\n(",["$","code",null,{"children":"?sentinelServiceName=mymaster"}],"; the default is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"master"}],"); pointing at a\nreplica directly gives read-only errors on write. For ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cluster"}],", any subset of\nnodes works and the client discovers the rest."]}]}],["$","$L43",null,{"title":"Two deployments are seeing each other's entries","id":"two-deployments-are-seeing-each-others-entries","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["They share a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"key_prefix"}],", or neither sets one. Give each deployment its own,\nor its own database index in the URL."]}]}]]}]
